course: dictionary
lesson: 69
title: Acorns and oak trees
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An acorn is the nut of an oak tree. It is smooth and oval, and it sits in a little rough cup. The words around a new word give you clues. «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts» tells you acorns are things you can pick up from the ground.
explain: Context can also show what something does. «Jays bury thousands of acorns each autumn to eat in winter» shows that acorns are stored as food for the cold months. Ask yourself what word would fit, then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words appear in sayings. «Mighty oaks from little acorns grow» means that big things often start small. Here the acorn is a picture of a small beginning, so read the whole saying to find the meaning.
fact: An acorn is the nut of an oak tree.
fact: Acorns are smooth and oval, and they sit in a little rough cup.
fact: «Squirrels» and «jays» bury acorns for winter, and they forget many of them.
fact: Acorns that are forgotten can grow into new oak trees.
fact: Acorns are poisonous, so you must never eat them.
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts.» What is an acorn? | *The nut of an oak tree | A type of squirrel | A kind of pine cone | A small brown bird
exercise: «Jays bury thousands of acorns each autumn to eat in winter.» Why do jays bury acorns? | To make a rough cup for their nests | To grow them into tall pine trees | *To store food for the winter | To keep the acorns warm at night
exercise: «Mighty oaks from little acorns grow.» What does this saying mean? | Squirrels eat acorns in winter | Oak trees are always very tall | *Big things often start small | Winter is coming soon
test: What is an acorn like? | Hairy and spiky | Sticky and red | *Smooth and oval | Long and thin
test: «Squirrels bury acorns and forget half of them, planting new oaks by accident.» What can a forgotten acorn grow into? | A brand new pond | *A new oak tree | A conker | A jay
exam: «Collect acorns for crafts, but never eat them, because they are poisonous.» Why must you never eat acorns? | Because they are too big to chew | *Because they are poisonous | Because squirrels need them all | Because they taste of sugar
